# Mandatory review on what nobody should change alone.
#
# This file only has an effect if `main`'s branch protection requires owner review —
# otherwise it is a suggestion. So it lists ONLY the paths where a mistake does not show
# in an ordinary review: a trust boundary, the delivery chain, or a promise made to the
# user.

# Default.
*                                   @tgaudibert

# ── The redaction engine ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# What decides what leaves in the clear. A weakened rule breaks no test that was not
# already written — which is exactly what makes the review indispensable.
/packages/redact/                   @tgaudibert

# ── The privileged process's boundaries ───────────────────────────────────────
# IPC, egress, secrets at rest, MCP gates, agent browser, Python sandbox — and the
# loopback OAuth broker the desktop spawns.
/apps/desktop/src/main/             @tgaudibert
/apps/desktop/src/preload/          @tgaudibert
/apps/mcp-broker/src/oauth/         @tgaudibert

# ── The delivery chain ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These files run with the repository's secrets, or decide what ships.
# `pnpm check:actions` already requires the SHA; review covers the rest.
/.github/                           @tgaudibert
/scripts/                           @tgaudibert
/pnpm-workspace.yaml                @tgaudibert
/pnpm-lock.yaml                     @tgaudibert

# ── The written promises ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECURITY.md is read by someone deciding whether to trust the product; a sentence that
# ages badly costs more than a bug there. Same for the hard rules.
/SECURITY.md                        @tgaudibert
/CLAUDE.md                          @tgaudibert
/README.md                          @tgaudibert
